      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Inline execution is chosen to spend less: it pays for one context (the executor's) plus one fresh final reviewer, instead of a fresh implementer and a fresh reviewer on every task that each re-read the codebase from zero. Core principle: the plan already did the thinking, so execute it exactly, prove each step with a test watched to fail then pass, and leave a ledger that survives context compaction. The plan-scoped workspace and ledger format are shared with subagent-driven-development (same directory, same format) so a plan can change executors mid-flight and resume from the same ledger."
    }
